\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Difference, in each school, between the mean release time of 1st-year EM classes and the mean release time of 2nd- and 3rd-year EM classes, morning shift (classes starting before 12:00), in 2013, 2014 and 2015. Positive values: the 1st year leaves later. Sample state schools with both 1st-year and 2nd- or 3rd-year morning classes in the year. \textbf  {Note:} the 19 schools that delayed 1st-year release by 50 minutes or more before 2014 (8 from 2011 to 2012 and 11 from 2012 to 2013) are excluded. The horizontal axis is cut at $-30$ and $80$ minutes, which leaves out 3 schools in 2013 (differences of $-120$, $-170$ and $-225$ minutes).}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
