\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {6}Release times by EM grade}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces DAG for the effect of concentration at release on the crime of 2nd- and 3rd-year EM students. Green: concentration mechanisms (1)--(4), numbered as in the Mechanisms subsection. Orange dashed: detection (9), which raises recorded crime without changing behaviour. Red: confounders that open back doors between concentration and crime (school level, individual sorting, time of day). Blue: the 2014 change in 1st-year schedules, which moves concentration for 2nd- and 3rd-year students without changing their own schedule, so it closes the time-of-day and hours-in-school paths for them; the red dashed arc is its main threat. The peer mechanisms (5)--(8) are not in this graph: in this design the students exposed are older than those added to the crowd.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:confounders}{{5}{11}{}{figure.5}{}}
